      "say": "R, reset, drives Q back to 0, and again it stays there. But look at the last box: if S and R are both 1, both outputs are forced to 0, which breaks the rule that Q and not Q are opposites. Release both together and the result is a race between the gates. So S equals R equals 1 is forbidden. How could a design make that impossible?",
